{
 "about": [
  "The ops-alert CONDITION contract, as data. (infra_an_ops_alert_is_a_condition_that_emails_once_when_it_starts_failing_and_once_when_it_recovers)",
  "BOTH implementations run every scenario here: the client (scripts/lib/ops_alert_machine.py, via scripts/lib/ops-alert.sh --self-test) and the API backstop (OpsAlertConditionMachine, via OpsAlertConditionMachineTests). One contract, two transports, one list of cases, so the two cannot drift apart unnoticed.",
  "PO RULING (Carl, 2026-09-28): SETTLED RECOVERY. [FAILING] at once; [RECOVERED] only once the key has stayed recovered for SETTLE (10 min); a re-fail inside the window cancels it silently; more than 4 transitions in 60 min sends ONE [FLAPPING], then nothing until it settles. \u26a0 SUPERSEDED 2026-09-29 where they conflict (Carl withdrew it for the owner-approved DECISIONS 2026-09-28 record): a key that has gone FLAPPING is released only by an HOUR of stability (FLAP_WINDOW); an ordinary failure keeps the 10-minute settle.",
  "Each step is {t: minutes since the scenario started, op: failing|recovered|tick}. `tick` is a scheduled settle check with no new reading (pr-refresh's 3-minute tick on the client, the hosted service on the server). expect lists every email the scenario sends, as [t, kind]."
 ],
